---
title: Select, range & file
description: The remaining controls — a native select with the system's chevron, a range whose track fills, a drop zone whose dashes march — and the search and number variations of an input.
eyebrow: Forms
source: src/components/field.css · src/js/im.js · im-media.js
---
<h2>Select</h2>
{{#example style="max-width: 26rem"}}
<div class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: .875rem">
	<div class="im-field"><label class="im-label" for="se-1">Topic</label><select class="im-select" id="se-1"><option>Design systems</option><option>Ghost themes</option><option>Travel</option></select></div>
	<div class="im-field"><label class="im-label" for="se-2">Grouped</label><select class="im-select" id="se-2"><optgroup label="Europe"><option>Budapest</option><option>Amsterdam</option></optgroup><optgroup label="Asia"><option>Kyoto</option></optgroup></select></div>
	<div class="im-field"><label class="im-label" for="se-3">Invalid</label><select class="im-select" id="se-3" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="se-3-e"><option value="">Choose one…</option><option>Monthly</option></select><p class="im-error" id="se-3-e">{{> "icons/circle-alert"}} Pick a plan to continue.</p></div>
	<select class="im-select im-input-sm" aria-label="Small" style="width: auto"><option>Newest first</option><option>Oldest first</option><option>Most read</option></select>
</div>
{{/example}}
<p><strong>It is the native <code>&lt;select&gt;</code></strong>, with our box and chevron. That is deliberate: the native list is the accessible one, and on a phone it opens the OS picker, which is better than anything drawn in HTML. For a menu of <em>actions</em> rather than a form value, use a <a href="/navigation/menu/">dropdown menu</a>.</p>

<h3>A dropdown that sets a value</h3>
<p>When the options need icons or descriptions, pair a button with a menu, and keep the value in a hidden input.</p>
{{#example center=true}}
<div>
	<input type="hidden" name="visibility" id="vis-value" value="public">
	<button class="im-btn im-btn-outline" type="button" popovertarget="vis-menu" aria-expanded="false" id="vis-btn">{{> "icons/globe"}} <span>Public</span> {{> "icons/chevron-down"}}</button>
	<div class="im-menu" id="vis-menu" popover data-align="start" onclick="const b=event.target.closest('[data-v]'); if(!b)return; document.getElementById('vis-value').value=b.dataset.v; document.querySelector('#vis-btn > span').textContent=b.querySelector('span').textContent; this.hidePopover()">
		<button class="im-menu-item" type="button" data-v="public">{{> "icons/globe"}}<span>Public</span><small>Everyone</small></button>
		<button class="im-menu-item" type="button" data-v="members">{{> "icons/users"}}<span>Members</span><small>Signed in</small></button>
		<button class="im-menu-item" type="button" data-v="paid">{{> "icons/lock"}}<span>Paid</span><small>Subscribers</small></button>
	</div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Range</h2>
{{#example style="max-width: 26rem"}}
<div class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 1.25rem">
	<div class="im-field"><label class="im-label" for="ra-1">Volume <output class="im-label-note" id="ra-1-o">40</output></label><input class="im-range" id="ra-1" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="40" oninput="document.getElementById('ra-1-o').textContent=this.value"></div>
	<div class="im-field"><label class="im-label" for="ra-2">Posts per page <output class="im-label-note" id="ra-2-o">12</output></label><input class="im-range" id="ra-2" type="range" min="6" max="48" step="6" value="12" oninput="document.getElementById('ra-2-o').textContent=this.value"></div>
</div>
{{/example}}
<p>The track fills up to the thumb — <code>im.js</code> keeps <code>--im-value</code> in step as it moves — and the thumb grows under the press. Show the number: a slider alone does not say what it is set to.</p>

<h2>File drop</h2>
{{#example style="max-width: 30rem"}}
<label class="im-drop">
	<input type="file" multiple>
	{{> "icons/upload"}}
	<strong>Drop files here, or click to choose</strong>
	<span data-im-drop-name="PNG, JPG or PDF — up to 10 MB">PNG, JPG or PDF — up to 10 MB</span>
</label>
{{/example}}
<p>A real <code>&lt;input type="file"&gt;</code> inside its label, so a click, the keyboard and a screen reader all work. <strong>The dashes march</strong> while you hover, focus, or drag a file over it (<code>im-media.js</code> sets <code>data-im-over</code>, fills the input from the drop, and writes the chosen names into <code>[data-im-drop-name]</code>).</p>

<h2>Search &amp; number</h2>
{{#example style="max-width: 26rem"}}
<div class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: .875rem">
	<div class="im-input-group">{{> "icons/search"}}<input class="im-input" type="search" placeholder="Search…" aria-label="Search"><kbd>/</kbd></div>
	<div class="im-input-group"><button class="im-btn im-btn-ghost im-btn-icon im-btn-sm" type="button" aria-label="Decrease" style="margin: 0 0 0 -.5rem" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.stepDown()">{{> "icons/minus"}}</button><input class="im-input text-center" type="number" value="2" min="1" max="9" aria-label="Seats"><button class="im-btn im-btn-ghost im-btn-icon im-btn-sm" type="button" aria-label="Increase" onclick="this.previousElementSibling.stepUp()">{{> "icons/plus"}}</button></div>
</div>
{{/example}}
